{"assets":[],"contestId":"1663","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"All problems were created and prepared by me and "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/magnus.hegdahl"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"magnus.hegdahl"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". Thanks to "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/BucketPotato"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BucketPotato"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Monogon"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Monogon"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Priyam2k"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Priyam2k"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" for valuable feedback and testing. Special thanks to "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" for coming up with the idea and preparing the unique checker for "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/H"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663H - Cross-Language Program"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". I hope you enjoyed the contest, and found it to be an interesting series of puzzles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example solution code written by "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Agnimandur"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Agnimandur"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" is provided for each problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663A - Who Tested?"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 1"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem statement is the title of the problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 2"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Re-read the original announcement blog."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If you carefully read "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/101364"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"the announcement blog"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", you will notice that I especially thanked "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/BucketPotato"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BucketPotato"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" for testing. Just print \"BucketPotato\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution Code (Python)"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"print(\"bucketpotato\")\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663B - Mike's Sequence"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 1"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Did you notice the peculiar constraints on the variable $$$r$$$?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 2"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\"Mike\" is of course "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". \"Mike's sequence\" has to do with Codeforces ratings."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 3"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3000 is the cutoff for the highest rating: Legendary Grandmaster."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mike's sequence are the Codeforces rating thresholds: [1200,1400,1600,1900,2100,2300,2400,2600,3000]. Your task is simply to print the threshold immediately above the provided rating $$$r$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution Code (Python)"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"R = int(input())\nratings = [1200,1400,1600,1900,2100,2300,2400,2600,3000]\nhigher = [r for r in ratings if r > R]\nprint(higher[0])\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663C - Pōja Verdon"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 1"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://awoiaf.westeros.org/index.php/Aenar_Targaryen"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aenar Targaryen"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" was a dragonlord of Old Valyria."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 2"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The main clue is the title: \"Pōja Verdon\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aenar Targaryen was a dragonlord of Valyria (an empire from a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A Song of Ice and Fire"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") who moved his family to Westeros right before Valyria was destroyed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pōja"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" means "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"their"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"verdon"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" means "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"sum"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" (or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"amount"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" based on context) in High Valyrian (you can easily translate this on "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://www.duolingo.com/dictionary/hv"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Duolingo"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a nutshell: Print the sum of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution Code (Python)"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"n = int(input())\nnums = list(map(int,input().strip().split()))\nprint(sum(nums))\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663D - Is it rated - 3"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 1"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Did you notice that the problem had a special \"constraints\" section? That's highly unusual for a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Codeforces"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 2"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The length of S is 3. Are there any famous three letter programming contests?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The capital variable letters and the \"constraints\" section are designed to mimic how "},{"attrs":{"href":"http://atcoder.jp"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"atcoder.jp"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" formats their problem statements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem is asking whether the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://atcoder.jp"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Atcoder contest"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" (ABC,ARC,AGC) is rated for a rating $$$X$$$. (Note that the judge ignores Atcoder heuristic contests for simplicity)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ABC's are rated for $$$[0,1999]$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ARC's are rated for $$$[0,2799]$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"AGC's are rated for $$$[1200,\\infty]$$$"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution Code (Python)"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"s = input().strip()\nx = int(input().strip())\nif (s==\"ABC\" and x<2000) or (s==\"ARC\" and x<2800) or (s==\"AGC\" and x>=1200):\n    print('yes')\nelse:\n    print('no')\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663E - Are You Safe?"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 1"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Do you recognize the story of the Minotaur?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 2"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem is a word search, but not for the word \"minotaur\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Perhaps you recognize the story of the minotaur? Less known is the hero who saved the kids from the minotaur: his name was Theseus [thee-see-us]."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem is just a word search (horizontal, vertical, diagonal) for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"theseus"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":". You should only go in the forward direction when you search for a word."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Bonus Clues (for other problems)"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The grid contains other clues embedded in it. Perhaps you can find "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"esoteric"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"java"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"script"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" (hints for problem G). You might be able to find "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"atcoder"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" (hint for problem D). Also "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"hero"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" (hinting at Theseus for this problem)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are also some red herring words out there."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution Code (C++)"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid good() {\n    cout << \"YES\";\n    exit(0);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int N; cin >> N;\n    char grid[N][N];\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        string row; cin >> row;\n        for (int j = 0; j < N; j++) grid[i][j] = row[j];\n    }\n\n    string word = \"theseus\";\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < N; j++) {\n\t\t\tif (i < N-7) {\n\t\t\t\tstring w = \"\";\n\t\t\t\tfor (int k = 0; k < 7; k++) w += grid[i+k][j];\n\t\t\t\tif (w == word) good();\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif (j < N-7) {\n\t\t\t\tstring w = \"\";\n\t\t\t\tfor (int k = 0; k < 7; k++) w += grid[i][j+k];\n\t\t\t\tif (w == word) good();\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif (i < N-7 && j < N-7) {\n\t\t\t\tstring w = \"\";\n\t\t\t\tfor (int k = 0; k < 7; k++) w += grid[i+k][j+k];\n\t\t\t\tif (w == word) good();\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n    }\n    cout << \"NO\";\n}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663F - In Every Generation..."}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 1"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Where is the quote from?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 2"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\"buffy\", \"the\", \"vampire\", \"slayer\""}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 3"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\"buffy\" (length 5), \"the\" (length 3), \"vampire\" (length 7), \"slayer\" (length 6). Remember how $$$3 \\le |s| \\le 7$$$? Now go back to the sample and see what you can do."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The quote is from the well known TV series "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buffy_the_Vampire_Slayer"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Buffy the Vampire Slayer"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Perhaps you notice the lengths of the words "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"buffy"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"the"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"vampire"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"slayer"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" are unique integers in the set {3,5,6,7}."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given the string $$$s$$$, simply \"add\" that string with the target word of the same length."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here's how adding two letters work:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Convert both letters to numbers in $$$[0,25]$$$."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Add the two numbers up modulo 26."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Convert the number back into a letter."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can verify your addition algorithm is correct by checking whether \"tourist\" + \"vampire\" = \"ooggqjx\" (as provided in the sample)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Finally, if the length of $$$s$$$ is $$$4$$$, the answer is \"none\", because there is no word of length 4 in Buffy the Vampire Slayer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution Code (Python)"}]},"children":[{"kind":"code_block","text":"s = input().strip()\nwords = [\"\",\"\",\"\",\"the\",\"\",\"buffy\",\"slayer\",\"vampire\"]\nif len(s)==4:\n    print(\"none\")\nelse:\n    target = words[len(s)]\n    ans = \"\"\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        a = ord(s[i])-ord('a')\n        b = ord(target[i])-ord('a')\n        ans += chr((a+b)%26 + ord('a'))\n    print(ans)\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/G"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663G - Six Characters"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 1"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input is a normal string of letters, but output consists of non-letter "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"characters"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 2"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Think of an esoteric programming language."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Clue 3"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSFuck"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"JSF"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" (an esoteric programming language equivalent to Javascript that only uses 6 characters)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The April Fool's Contests love of esoteric programming languages, combined with the reference to \"six characters\", will eventually lead you to JSFuck."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The six characters is a pun: the input is a string of length 6 like \"abcdef\", but the output is a string \\textit{consisting} of only 6 characters: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[ ] ( ) ! +"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Brief research will demonstrate a mapping from each english letter to a JSFuck string. Two letters can be concatenated with \"+\".Note that the optimal mapping will make your solution file approximately 12KB in size, well within the 64KB requirement of Codeforces."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, the mapping from each letter to javascript is not unique! However, the legend mentions that Aenar needs to go to the string's \"home\". JSFuck's home website is "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://jsfuck.com"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"here"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", which is where the jury's mapping is created from."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alternatively, instead of hardcoding the generated strings, you can simply use the encoding algorithm provided in the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://github.com/aemkei/jsfuck"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Github"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution Code (Python and Javascript)"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hard-coding strings: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/submission/152393980"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"152393980"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Algorithmically generating strings (in Javascript): "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/submission/152398972"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"152398972"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" (credit to "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/BigDelta"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BigDelta"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"spoiler"},{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1663/problem/H"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1663H - Cross-Language Program"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"title":[{"kind":"text","text":"Solution"}]},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Google research into how Pascal and C++ work will eventually lead you to a solution like this. Many people used the fact that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\\"}],"kind":"inline_code"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be used to continue single line comments to the next line in C++ but not in Pascal."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"// \\\nbegin end.\nint main() {}\n"}],"kind":"spoiler"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/101494"}